 560: 
 561: if __name__ == "__main__":
 562:     main()

codex
- Line 291 — merged/count error. Input to `introduction()`: `{"question":"Q?","results":{"by_outcome":{"a":{"k":1,"pooled":{"point":1},"per_trial":[{"trial_id":"NCT1","n":100}]},"b":{"k":1,"pooled":{"point":2},"per_trial":[{"trial_id":"NCT1","n":100}]}}}}`. Consequence: one 100-participant trial is reported as 200 participants.

- Line 225 — selector keyed to the wrong field. Input to `references()`: `{"inputs":{"trials":[{"nct":"NCT1"}]},"published_comparison":{"reviews":[{"journal":"BMJ","year":2024,"pmid":"123"}]}}`. Consequence: the record is both cited as `BMJ. 2024.` and named in the note as carrying “NO title, journal or year.”

- Line 328 — zero conflated with absent. Input to `introduction()`: `{"question":"Q?","results":{"by_outcome":{"o":{"k":1,"pooled":{"point":0.0},"per_trial":[{"trial_id":"NCT1","n":0}]}}}}`. Consequence: a recorded zero participant count is suppressed exactly like a missing count.

- Line 529 — check that cannot fail after normal return. Input to `bookkeeping()`: `({}, "__no_appraisal_files__")`, with no matching `ssot/__no_appraisal_files__/appraisal/*.json`. Consequence: `len(bk) > 1` is still true because registration absence and second-assessor absence are always written, so “bookkeeping on” can report success while search, limb, and RoB-domain claims are absent.

- Line 540 — status reports buildability, not work done. Input file for `main --all t`: `{"question":"Q?","manuscript":{"introduction":"existing"},"results":{"by_outcome":{"o":{"k":1,"pooled":{"point":1},"per_trial":[]}}}}`. Consequence: line 522 skips the write, but `display_change_announced.what_changed` still says `introduction written`.

